5. Scheduling in Prod — Confirmed

What runs when:

Table/Pipeline	Schedule
All main tables	Weekly (Saturday — spread throughout)
Account Summary	Daily
Account Snapshot	Daily (only pulls if delta exists — no data = just latest watermark, fast)
TXN_PLAN_MONTH_AGG (Count TXN)	Daily
Closure + Enrollment	Weekly (confirm with BI team)
Everything else	Move to weekly once stable

Key insight on Snapshot:

Snapshot only loads once a month (2nd day of month)
But running daily is fine because:
→ If no delta → pipeline just sees latest watermark
→ Pulls nothing → completes instantly
→ No wasted compute on empty runs

Scheduling approach:

Run 8 AM Saturday for most tables
Spread tables throughout Saturday
Keep daily: Account Summary, Snapshot, TXN Count
Once BI team confirms → finalize schedule
6. Deployment Pipeline Ownership Issue

Problem:

Whoever runs the deployment pipeline
→ Becomes OWNER of all objects inside it
→ Including ALL objects in production workspace
→ If that person leaves → ownership problem

Solution:

Use Microsoft Service Account to run deployments
→ Log out of personal account
→ Log in as service account
→ Run deployment pipeline
→ Service account owns everything in Prod
→ Not tied to any individual person
→ Team can share service account credentials
